   and next to it `10-today` (a weather screen behind the tile), `20-fetch` (fastfetch as a dashboard), `45-terminal` (a live terminal) and
   `60-owl` (sprites).
+
+### Header controls (owl 8)
+
+A screen may contain one optional `header { ... }` block. Its compact nodes render in the window title row immediately before the launcher's close control, sharing widget state and handlers. Existing screens without a header are unchanged. Keep it to a few fixed-size controls; avoid terminals, scrolling lists, or full-width content in this row. Declare `meta { owl: 8 }` so older launchers request an update.
+
+```owl
+widget "Header example" {
+  meta { owl: 8 }
+  state settings = false
+  Text { text: "Open"; onTap: screen() }
+  screen {
+    title: "Miilo"
+    header {
+      Text { text: "⚙"; fontSize: 24; width: 44; height: 44; align: center; onTap: settings = !settings }
+    }
+    Text { text: settings ? "Settings" : "Work" }
+  }
+}
+```
